y_caller":"Andy Reid"},{"season":2024,"team":"SEA","distance":1.157,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"ARI","distance":0.364,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Nick Rallis"},{"season":2025,"team":"LA","distance":0.4101,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Chris Shula"},{"season":2025,"team":"PHI","distance":0.4391,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vic Fangio"},{"season":2024,"team":"BAL","distance":0.5065,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"TEN","distance":0.5325,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Bengals are 7-2 through week 10 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 278 to 193. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 2nd in EPA per play while the defense sits 15th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive traits are the highest pass rate over expected and the 2nd fewest defenders in the box in the league.","offense":"The Bengals offense has been one of the best in the league by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better passing the ball than running it. They have thrown more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score has not called for it. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the lowest play-action rate and the highest shotgun rate in the league. Joe Burrow has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Ja'Marr Chase, who has drawn 26% of the targets.","defense":"The Bengals defense has been about average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 11th and 26th. Boye Mafe leads the team with 6.5 sacks, and Dexter Lawrence has added 5, after not being a regular on this defense last season. In terms of scheme, they have the 2nd fewest defenders in the box in the league.","special":"The Bengals have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 23% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 93% of field goals, which is well above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into receivers, about 22% of the money on the books. Their quarterbacks were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Joe Burrow has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,795 yards. Ja'Marr Chase has been the clear top target with 26% of the looks and 878 receiving yards. Chase Brown has handled most of the work in the backfield with 65% of the carries. On defense, Boye Mafe leads the team with 6.5 sacks and Jordan Battle has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Zac Taylor is calling the offense as head coach and Al Golden is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Commanders and the 2025 Chiefs under Andy Reid. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Cardinals under Nick Rallis and the 2025 Rams under Chris Shula.","trends":"The offense went from 19th in EPA per play in 2025 to 2nd so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 29th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 15th so far this season, a big step forward. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 10% to 3%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}